Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:38:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 425/488] [DS4.1] Greedy shard pairs in 16-byte rows, gathered
 in place

The drafter's five greedy steps and the all-greedy verification gather
each rank's (max, index) pair across the vocabulary shards. As [rows, 2]
FP32 (8-byte rows) they took the one-shot all-gather's padded path: a
staging copy and a reshape copy around every gather, ten graph kernels a
decode step and two eager ones. The pairs now sit in the first two
columns of [rows, 4] rows, which the gather writes straight into the
concatenated layout; the finish writes at the pairs' row stride and the
selection reads each rank's pair at its width.
